From f282cfe879a93c82f1f09a0200fe119fdb48e32e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zak Wilson <zak.wilson@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:18:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cheader: skip an attribute after a function's return type

GCC admits an attribute between a declaration's return type and its name,
where Lua's `l_noret` puts `__attribute__((noreturn))`, so every error
function in Lua's internal headers (luaG_runerror, luaD_throw) was skipped
with `__attribute__` read as the name. c-parse-func-decl now skips that
attribute run too (nuc-lua ISSUE-026). `lua-header-shapes` covers it.

That makes clang intrinsics with `__DEFAULT_FN_ATTRS` in that place
readable, and `_mm512_set_epi8` has 64 parameters, so C-MAX-PARAMS is 64
and `w3b-skip`'s fixture is widened to 65.

Gate: nuctests 1740 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped; bootstrap fixed point holds.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CsC8i2S7yJAHSpzRaddMj3
