diff --git a/design/progress.md b/design/progress.md
index e8457d54..f1121f30 100644
--- a/design/progress.md
+++ b/design/progress.md
@@ -5740,3 +5740,15 @@ dead temporary. nuc-doom ISSUE-040 had fixed this for a binding receiver only.
 
 `s21-array-field-of-nested-place` covers struct and union members, `field`, and an
 element receiver.
+
+## Lua-port fixes: an attribute after the return type (lua-bugfixes)
+
+Found by the nuc-lua port (its ISSUE-026): Lua's `l_noret` expands to `void
+__attribute__((noreturn))`, so every error function in its internal headers
+(`luaG_runerror`, `luaD_throw`) was skipped: `__attribute__` read as the name.
+`c-parse-func-decl` now skips an attribute run after the return type, as it already
+did before the declaration and after the parameters. `lua-header-shapes` covers it.
+
+That makes clang's intrinsics readable where `__DEFAULT_FN_ATTRS` sat between the type
+and the name, and `_mm512_set_epi8` takes 64 parameters: `C-MAX-PARAMS` is now 64, so
+`w3b-sdl` stays silent.
diff --git a/docs/structs-unions.md b/docs/structs-unions.md
index 63d8b66e..f0062354 100644
--- a/docs/structs-unions.md
+++ b/docs/structs-unions.md
@@ -781,7 +781,9 @@ site emits.
 ## Recognized libc function attributes: `noreturn` and `returns_twice`
 
 A C header carries no attribute metadata the importer trusts — even an
-explicit `__attribute__((noreturn))` is discarded — so a small set of
+explicit `__attribute__((noreturn))` is discarded, wherever GCC admits it: before
+the declaration, after it, or between the return type and the name (`void
+__attribute__((noreturn)) f(void);`, Lua's `l_noret`) — so a small set of
 well-known libc functions is recognized **by name** instead and gets the
 matching LLVM attribute on its `declare`: `exit`, `abort`, `_exit`, `_Exit`,
 `quick_exit`, `abort_handler_s`, `longjmp` and `siglongjmp` get `noreturn` (a
diff --git a/src/cheader.nuc b/src/cheader.nuc
index 506ae2ad..5ab39a32 100644
--- a/src/cheader.nuc
+++ b/src/cheader.nuc
@@ -867,7 +867,8 @@
 ; and the gate's cap: a declaration with more parameters than this is skipped
 ; rather than silently truncated. Before W3b the array was 16 entries and
 ; `num-params` was incremented past it, so `type-set-params` read off the end.
-(defconst C-MAX-PARAMS 32)
+; 64 is clang's widest, `_mm512_set_epi8`.
+(defconst C-MAX-PARAMS 64)
 
 ; Record that `fname`'s declaration was skipped, and — when `loud` — say so on
 ; stderr immediately. `g-cheader-skipped` (declared in nucleusc.nuc, above
@@ -1358,7 +1359,9 @@
     ; C decays an array in a parameter or return position; a struct MEMBER keeps
     ; its extent, which is why the call is here and not in c-parse-type.
     (set! ret-type (as ptr (array-decay ret-type)))
-    (set! pos (c-skip-ws buf pos len))
+    ; GCC admits attributes between the return type and the name, where Lua's
+    ; `l_noret` puts `__attribute__((noreturn))`; they read as the name otherwise.
+    (set! pos (c-skip-attributes buf pos len))
     (when (and (< pos len) (= (cstr-byte-at buf pos) 40))
       (let (fr:i32 (c-parse-fnret-decl buf pos len ret-type out-end decl-start))
         (when (>= fr 0) (return fr))))
